title: Genesis 24 – A Wife for Isaac
description: A verse-by-verse study of Genesis 24: Abraham sends his eldest servant to his kindred, the prayer at the well, Rebekah draws for the camels, the LORD led me, I will go, and Isaac takes Rebekah to wife.
output: lessons/genesis/genesis-24-a-wife-for-isaac.html
context: Genesis 24

# Genesis series pattern (Genesis 1-5). Slide text is the author's own words from the Genesis 24 study (post 7157,
# 15 December 2022), set in chapter order; the study is short, so most of the chapter is read through without a
# paragraph, as the pattern has it where the author said nothing on the verses.
# Fixed: nothing; the study was clean.

=== Introduction
--- Genesis Chapter 24 [title]
overline: Young Adult Sunday School • Genesis Series
heading: Genesis 24: A Wife for Isaac
sub: The Eldest Servant • The Well • Rebekah • I Will Go • Isaac Comforted
refs: Genesis 24:1-67
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any reference to read the verse.

=== The oath
--- Put Thy Hand under My Thigh
kicker: vv. 1–4
sub: Unto My Country, and to My Kindred
scripture: Genesis 24:1-4 | mark: the LORD had blessed Abraham in all things; take a wife unto my son Isaac

--- He Shall Send His Angel before Thee
kicker: vv. 5–9
sub: Bring Not My Son Thither Again
scripture: Genesis 24:5-9 | mark: he shall send his angel before thee
p: The faith of Abraham and the servant brought Isaac a wife in Rebekah. In uncertain times and strange lands, leading the servant to where he needed to be.

=== At the well
--- Send Me Good Speed This Day
kicker: vv. 10–14
sub: The Time That Women Go Out to Draw Water
scripture: Genesis 24:10-14 | mark: O LORD God of my master Abraham, I pray thee, send me good speed this day

--- Before He Had Done Speaking
kicker: vv. 15–18
sub: Drink, My Lord
scripture: Genesis 24:15-18 | mark: before he had done speaking, that, behold, Rebekah came out

--- I Will Draw Water for Thy Camels Also
kicker: vv. 19–21
sub: Whether the LORD Had Made His Journey Prosperous
scripture: Genesis 24:19-21 | mark: I will draw water for thy camels also

--- Whose Daughter Art Thou?
kicker: vv. 22–25
sub: Room to Lodge In
scripture: Genesis 24:22-25 | mark: Whose daughter art thou?

--- I Being in the Way, the LORD Led Me
kicker: vv. 26–27
sub: The Man Bowed Down His Head
scripture: Genesis 24:26-27 | mark: I being in the way, the LORD led me

--- Seek Their Rebekah
kicker: Application • Genesis 24:27
sub: Trusting in the Lord to Guide Them
p: So many young men seek their Rebekah, and go where they should not, doing what they should not and not trusting in the Lord to guide them.
p: But Abraham knew in faith such a thing was possible. I am firmly convinced of the same, with the longview of being an old head and seeing God's angels bringing me where I needed to be, and watching faith move in other's lives the same way.
p: Don't be discouraged. And young ladies seeking a spouse, live Godly with hospitality, grace and kindness, and the man for you will show himself.
p: Amen.

=== Laban
--- Come In, Thou Blessed of the LORD
kicker: vv. 28–31
sub: Rebekah Had a Brother
scripture: Genesis 24:28-31 | mark: Come in, thou blessed of the LORD

--- I Will Not Eat, until I Have Told Mine Errand
kicker: vv. 32–33
sub: Speak On
scripture: Genesis 24:32-33 | mark: I will not eat, until I have told mine errand

=== The servant's errand
--- I Am Abraham's Servant
kicker: vv. 34–38
sub: The LORD Hath Blessed My Master Greatly
scripture: Genesis 24:34-38 | mark: I am Abraham’s servant

--- The LORD, before Whom I Walk
kicker: vv. 39–41
sub: Will Send His Angel with Thee
scripture: Genesis 24:39-41 | mark: will send his angel with thee, and prosper thy way

--- If Now Thou Do Prosper My Way
kicker: vv. 42–44
sub: Let the Same Be the Woman
scripture: Genesis 24:42-44 | mark: let the same be the woman whom the LORD hath appointed out for my master’s son

--- Before I Had Done Speaking in Mine Heart
kicker: vv. 45–48
sub: Which Had Led Me in the Right Way
scripture: Genesis 24:45-48 | mark: before I had done speaking in mine heart; which had led me in the right way

--- The Thing Proceedeth from the LORD
kicker: vv. 49–51
sub: Take Her, and Go
scripture: Genesis 24:49-51 | mark: The thing proceedeth from the LORD

=== I will go
--- He Worshipped the LORD
kicker: vv. 52–53
sub: Jewels of Silver, and Jewels of Gold
scripture: Genesis 24:52-53 | mark: he worshipped the LORD, bowing himself to the earth

--- Hinder Me Not
kicker: vv. 54–56
sub: Seeing the LORD Hath Prospered My Way
scripture: Genesis 24:54-56 | mark: Hinder me not, seeing the LORD hath prospered my way

--- I Will Go
kicker: vv. 57–61
sub: Wilt Thou Go with This Man?
scripture: Genesis 24:57-61 | mark: Wilt thou go with this man? And she said, I will go

=== Isaac
--- Isaac Went Out to Meditate in the Field
kicker: vv. 62–65
sub: It Is My Master
scripture: Genesis 24:62-65 | mark: Isaac went out to meditate in the field at the eventide

--- Isaac Was Comforted
kicker: vv. 66–67
sub: And He Loved Her
scripture: Genesis 24:66-67 | mark: and he loved her: and Isaac was comforted after his mother’s death

--- Preparing the Way
center: An angel of the Lord lighting the path and preparing the way.
